# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored) for local development,
# and set the same keys in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables
# for production (and Preview). VITE_* values are baked into the bundle at
# build time, so a change only takes effect after a redeploy.

# ── Required in production ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Web3Forms access key — delivers contact-form leads by email (src/utils/leads.ts).
# Leads go to whichever inbox registered the key at https://web3forms.com,
# so register it with info.1618digital@gmail.com. The key is public by
# design (it ends up in the client bundle); it is kept here only so it is
# configured in one place. A production build on Vercel FAILS without it
# (see vite.config.ts) — the form once shipped without a key and silently
# dropped every inquiry for weeks.
VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY=

# Temporary escape hatch, Vercel only: "true" lets production build without
# the key, with the form offering WhatsApp/email only. Ignored once the key
# is set — delete it then. No VITE_ prefix: it never reaches the bundle.
# LEAD_FALLBACK_ONLY=

# ── Optional ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leaving either blank simply skips that provider (see
# src/utils/thirdPartyAnalytics.ts). Neither script loads for a visitor
# until they click "Alle Akzeptieren" in the cookie banner.

# Google Analytics 4 — Measurement ID from
# Google Analytics → Admin → Data Streams → your web stream (format: G-XXXXXXXXXX)
VITE_GA4_ID=

# Meta (Facebook/Instagram) Pixel ID from
# Meta Events Manager → Data Sources → your pixel (numeric ID)
VITE_META_PIXEL_ID=
